3SHOW v3.1.1                                             John Elliott, 6-3-2001
===============================================================================

  3SHOW is a drop-in replacement for the CP/M Plus SHOW utility. It has the
following features:

* Program is 8k in size; original CP/M DIR is 9k.
* All options from the original SHOW are valid.
* Piping and redirection of output (via PIPEMGR) is supported. If this is
 not required, you can remove the RSX with:

   GENCOM 3DIR

  which will reduce program size to 5k.

New in 3SHOW 3.1.1
==================

* Options can be separated by commas or white space or both, eg:

    3SHOW [SPACE USERS]

Differences from CP/M 3 SHOW
============================

* Output redirection: You can use:

    3SHOW {opts} >filename    Write to file
    3SHOW {opts} >>filename   Append to existing file
    3SHOW {opts} |program     Send output through a PIPEMGR filter

    Filenames in the ">" and ">>" options can contain user numbers - eg:
   10A:file.typ  or  B6:list.txt. These options also accept the device
   names CON: LST: AUX: and NUL: 

* Date output is fully Year 2000 compliant and uses a 4-digit year. 

* In SHOW, the result of 

   SHOW B:[USERS]

  was different from 
 
   SHOW B: [USERS]

  In 3SHOW, these both behave like the first command. 
